{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh","id":1308322,"title":"Armored Flesh!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-27T10:27:25-07:00","id":1308322,"title":"Armored Flesh!?","content":"Ok, since I've seen this power in the V20 Dark Ages Vampire core book (some years ago) I dismissed it as pure bad writting and decided to create some different power using some actual mechanics. But in any case, while I tend to prefer using the original rules for powers listed in the books, I couldn't fail to notice that this power is just terrible beyond redemption (perhaps even worse than that &quot;Arm of Prometheus&quot; of Dark Ages Vampire...but I'm still not sure which one is worse, they are both good contenders lol).<br /> A level 8 power that has a nice idea that your character is basically invulnerable while it's in use usw. it mentions that your character can &quot;touch white hot metals without suffering harm&quot;, but it has no combat use!? What!? The text clearly ruins an interesting and terribly scary power idea when it states &quot;...Outside of combat situations your character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures, blades or impacts...&quot; I mean what the hell? What's wrong? What is the point of this power? Come on, it makes absolutely no sense in any metaphysical understanding you can think of. But ok, life goes on...<br /> The point of this thread (besides the fact that I'm on &quot;forced vacation&quot; after making a surgery and thus I don't have many things to do lol) is to ask you guys your opinion on the power and more importantly, what rules would you use for it during combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-27-2019, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:54:38-07:00","id":1308332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spend two blood points to activate Armored<br /> Flesh for the scene. Outside of combat situations, your<br /> character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures,<br /> blades, or impacts. While a tongue of flame will still affect<br /> her, she can forge softened metals with her bare hands. </div> </div> </div>This seems to be the out of combat section<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her unarmed attacks cause Strength + Fortitude in bashing damage.<br /> Lastly, she may block any bashing, lethal, or aggravated<br /> attack with her bare hands. </div> </div> </div>And this is the in combat effect.<br /> <br /> You can be a blacksmith without needing tools or protection would be the tl;dr of the power<br /> <br /> Fortitude powers have always been awful though, aside from cool factor, the soak die is pretty much always the better option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:59:11-07:00","id":1308333,"title":"","content":"Rules during combat: &quot;Dude, you've got 7 other levels of Fortitude. What more do you need?&quot;<br /> <br /> The power is effectively a blanket statement of &quot;Barring supernatural vulnerabilities and combat, forget your health levels for a scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308332#post1308332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortitude powers have always been awful though, aside from cool factor, the soak die is pretty much always the better option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, shattering enemy weapons on impact or bestowing your Fortitude on others sounds pretty cool to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 04-27-2019, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:15:03-07:00","id":1308335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308333#post1308333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules during combat: &quot;Dude, you've got 7 other levels of Fortitude. What more do you need?&quot;<br /> <br /> The power is effectively a blanket statement of &quot;Barring supernatural vulnerabilities and combat, forget your health levels for a scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eh, shattering enemy weapons on impact or bestowing your Fortitude on others sounds pretty cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that makes no sense! It doesn't make ANY sense! How can you be nigh invulnerable to harm in a moment, but then you are vulnerable if it's a &quot;combat scene&quot;? Besides the ability to block attacks and the non-sense of adding fortitude level to your unarmed attacks is way too lame even for a level 5 power. We are talking about a level 8 power! With that level I can kill someone with a look or dominate anyone I know not matter where this person is...Not to mention celerity level 8 that allows me to basically come back in time to avoid any harm...and it matters not the other levels of powers, because with any freaking discipline you're going to have the previous powers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:17:27-07:00","id":1308337,"title":"","content":"Armor of Kings is good, true. The Blessings of vitality is also ok to me, but this one is a contender for the worst power ever created (although obternebration and abyss mysticism powers of giving a two way ticket to abysm are good contenders...). See the problem is not only the system, but SPECIALLY that it is non-sensical in the metaphysical sense of the word. How come it has no effect during combats? It should be worded as it has a duration and so on, but not that it has an effect &quot;outside combat&quot; and during combat because it makes no sense, the characters are not transported to another dimension where the laws of reality are different when they engage combat and THAT is the main point of my complain. Is not only being weak systematically talking...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-27-2019, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:24:34-07:00","id":1308339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308333#post1308333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, shattering enemy weapons on impact or bestowing your Fortitude on others sounds pretty cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool is all they are though. If someone's not doing enough damage for Knight's Bane to shatter the weapon, it shattering is kind of moot, you have to soak all the damage from (Melee+dex)-1 + str + Potence + Weapon damage... Lending out Fort, eh, maybe cornercase useful, but again, not night to night very great.<br /> <br /> The best soak powers are in Protean and Serpentus, just buy Fortitude for the dice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:25:26-07:00","id":1308341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308335#post1308335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that makes no sense! It doesn't make ANY sense! How can you be nigh invulnerable to harm in a moment, but then you are vulnerable if it's a &quot;combat scene&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about a mystic ability, so my explanation would be: A mindless force of nature is easier to shield against than killing intent. Take a look at Shadowrun and its rules for spirit combat, where melee weapons rule because rifles and rockets are too far removed from the will of their user to work against spirits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:33:28-07:00","id":1308347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308339#post1308339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool is all they are though. If someone's not doing enough damage for Knight's Bane to shatter the weapon, it shattering is kind of moot, you have to soak all the damage from (Melee+dex)-1 + str + Potence + Weapon damage...</div> </div> </div> </div>Noone says the attack has to fully go through. Parry it, take away all but one success on the hit and let your armor, your stamina and your Fortitude do the rest - transform your Fortitude dice into auto-succeses if you have to. All you need is one sub-par die roll from your attacker and they're disarmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308339#post1308339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lending out Fort, eh, maybe cornercase useful, but again, not night to night very great.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The entire coterie and all their retainers gain Fortitude 5+&quot; is not so much &quot;cornercase useful&quot; as &quot;borderline broken&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:53:23-07:00","id":1308352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308341#post1308341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about a mystic ability, so my explanation would be: A mindless force of nature is easier to shield against than killing intent. Take a look at Shadowrun and its rules for spirit combat, where melee weapons rule because rifles and rockets are too far removed from the will of their user to work against spirits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again I think it's too weak for its description and makes no sense imo as characters are still real and in the physical world where they should be subject to its rules,i,e, the characters are not transported to another dimension when they engage combat. If someone launches a missile at your character during a &quot;non-combat scene&quot; it would work, but as soon as &quot;the combat starts&quot; it is useless for defense? It doesn't make sense imo. I'm thinking about using V5 Fortitude 5 power that completelly ignores the first source of damage your character would suffer every turn. Interestingly the power is named after the Protean Skin of Marble power. In any case the system is good and I'm considering using it for Armored Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T12:12:05-07:00","id":1308361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308339#post1308339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool is all they are though. If someone's not doing enough damage for Knight's Bane to shatter the weapon, it shattering is kind of moot, you have to soak all the damage from (Melee+dex)-1 + str + Potence + Weapon damage... Lending out Fort, eh, maybe cornercase useful, but again, not night to night very great.<br /> <br /> The best soak powers are in Protean and Serpentus, just buy Fortitude for the dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why i like to use the houserule suggested in a dark ages book that now I fail to remember, since I've been using it for more than 15 years, so essencially I allow Stamina + Fortitude to soak most sources of damage, including aggravated with basically a few exceptions like fire and sunlight and a few other damages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:39:54-07:00","id":1308376,"title":"","content":"From Dark Ages Vampire core;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike normal Cainites - who cannot soak sunlight or other aggravated damage at all - Fortitude users can roll Stamina + Fortitude to soak damage from sunlight and fire </div> </div> </div>Not a house rule, and the best reason any Cainite could want to pick up at least a dot...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:46:14-07:00","id":1308377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308376#post1308376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From Dark Ages Vampire core;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not a house rule, and the best reason any Cainite could want to pick up at least a dot...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it was suggested in an earlier book before Dark Ages Vampire, I'm not sure if it was in the first dark ages . This one you mention I remember from Dark Ages: Vampire, but I always thought it was somehow wrong as according to this it would be easier to a vampire to soak aggravated damage from fire and sunlight (that are vampire's weakeness) than from a claw for instance. So i usually rule that you soak aggravated damage from most sources with stamina + fortitude and fire and sunlught only with fortitude. Or do you mean that you allow vampires to soak EVERY kind of aggravated damage with stamina + fortitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:52:21-07:00","id":1308380,"title":"","content":"No, just Fortitude for most Agg, but fire and sunlight you get the full whack of Sta+Fort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T14:05:29-07:00","id":1308384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1308380#post1308380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, just Fortitude for most Agg, but fire and sunlight you get the full whack of Sta+Fort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, as I said before imo it makes no sense. How on earth should a vampire fear the claw (or the thaumaturgy lv 2 ritual on a sword or so many many other kinds of aggravated damage in WoD) more than fire and sunlight that are vampire banes?<br /> <br /> Imo it was a huge oversight in DAV that fortunately they didn't repeat in DAV20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-27-2019, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:24:08-07:00","id":1482341,"title":"","content":"I'm still open for ideas here, btw. I wanted a system to fix this power and I'd prefer to discuss it with people than creating it myself, as I'm feeling lonely and in need of care lol (I hate sundays)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T11:35:41-07:00","id":1482388,"title":"","content":"My understanding was that the power only affected the vampire's hands(probably dubious reading on my part), but I feel that is probably the way this makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> It essentially mean your vamps Hands are immune to blades, fire, and mundane damage, which is why you can block weapons and do ridiculous bashing damage unarmed, but the opponent can still stab you in the chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T14:49:56-07:00","id":1482408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482388#post1482388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding was that the power only affected the vampire's hands(probably dubious reading on my part), but I feel that is probably the way this makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> It essentially mean your vamps Hands are immune to blades, fire, and mundane damage, which is why you can block weapons and do ridiculous bashing damage unarmed, but the opponent can still stab you in the chest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The power clearly states &quot;Your character's skin is like steel and is just as durable&quot;, also &quot;Outside of combat situations, your character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures, blades, or impacts. &quot; It doesn't state at any point that it only affects your hands (or feet, as they also gain supernatural extra damage), btw making it only affect your hand would make it another <i>Arm of Prometheus</i>, but worse.<br /> So the part that doesn't make any sense is: &quot;Outside of combat situations, your character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures, blades, or impacts. &quot;, my point here is to come up with an acceptable system for this power in order to make it any good. I want to avoid simply declaring that the character is completely invulnerable for the duration of the power, as it would be a bit &quot;boring&quot;, so I'm here asking for suggestions for a good system to use with this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T01:06:09-07:00","id":1482466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482408#post1482408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The power clearly states &quot;Your character's skin is like steel and is just as durable&quot;, also &quot;Outside of combat situations, your character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures, blades, or impacts. &quot; It doesn't state at any point that it only affects your hands (or feet, as they also gain supernatural extra damage), btw making it only affect your hand would make it another <i>Arm of Prometheus</i>, but worse.<br /> So the part that doesn't make any sense is: &quot;Outside of combat situations, your character suffers no damage from mundane temperatures, blades, or impacts. &quot;, my point here is to come up with an acceptable system for this power in order to make it any good. I want to avoid simply declaring that the character is completely invulnerable for the duration of the power, as it would be a bit &quot;boring&quot;, so I'm here asking for suggestions for a good system to use with this power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A quick fix could be to make the power transform all de damage in bashing damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T08:24:03-07:00","id":1482493,"title":"","content":"You could take a clue from requiem and the juggernaut devotion, after the fixed starting cost to activate the discipline, you have to spend blood every turn to mantain it, this to balance the fact that FUCK EVERYONE, I'M INVULNERABLE, basically have the power give you complete invulnerability for as long as you can sustain it's cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T10:52:06-07:00","id":1482507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482493#post1482493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could take a clue from requiem and the juggernaut devotion, after the fixed starting cost to activate the discipline, you have to spend blood every turn to mantain it, this to balance the fact that FUCK EVERYONE, I'M INVULNERABLE, basically have the power give you complete invulnerability for as long as you can sustain it's cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's nice, where can I find it? The idea of using blood to keep the power active is something I thought about, but where can I find such devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T10:56:27-07:00","id":1482508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482507#post1482507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's nice, where can I find it? The idea of using blood to keep the power active is something I thought about, but where can I find such devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's in the vampire the requiem 2nd edition core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:08:50-07:00","id":1482509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A quick fix could be to make the power transform all de damage in bashing damage </div> </div> </div>That's certainly an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It's in the vampire the requiem 2nd edition core book.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Thank you very much!</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:15:50-07:00","id":1482511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482509#post1482509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's certainly an option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you very much![/FONT]<br /> [/FONT]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are welcome, devotions are a pretty good way to develop powers for masquerade, hell you could actually port some of them as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:36:02-07:00","id":1482516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482511#post1482511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are welcome, devotions are a pretty good way to develop powers for masquerade, hell you could actually port some of them as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes indeed! I might have a look at it, seems promising, and it's even very weird that we never had a similar power in Vampire after so many years. I was always amazed at how lackluster most Fortitude powers are in VtM, it's almost as they did that on purpose lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:45:10-07:00","id":1482518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482516#post1482516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes indeed! I might have a look at it, seems promising, and it's even very weird that we never had a similar power in Vampire after so many years. I was always amazed at how lackluster most Fortitude powers are in VtM, it's almost as they did that on purpose lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Requiem vamps are both weaker and tougher than masquerade (V20 of course, not V5) vamps, they get more starting bennies and their disciplines are generally more useful (fortitude in requiem pretty much makes you unkillable unless sunlight, a mage or a nuke are involved and that's without devotions) but on the other hand their physical intensity only adds 2 dice per vitae spent on rolls and resistances and lasts only 1 turn while masquerade vamps can pump their attributes to 6 dots for a whole scene and there is no power that can match masquerade elders plot device disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:03:40-07:00","id":1482521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482518#post1482518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Requiem vamps are both weaker and tougher than masquerade (V20 of course, not V5) vamps, they get more starting bennies and their disciplines are generally more useful (fortitude in requiem pretty much makes you unkillable unless sunlight, a mage or a nuke are involved and that's without devotions) but on the other hand their physical intensity only adds 2 dice per vitae spent on rolls and resistances and lasts only 1 turn while masquerade vamps can pump their attributes to 6 dots for a whole scene and there is no power that can match masquerade elders plot device disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems interesting, the part of elders powers that doesn't make much sense in masquerade, I mean with Dominate 8 I can dominate any person in the world, one could dominate Biden and tell him to do anything I in the confort of my coffin, while a vampire with Fortitude 8 might still struggle in combat against a pack of Garous or gangrels, all because the system failed to come up with any decent power for the discipline level. I don't know much about Requiem, but the more I heard from it lately, the more I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:29:03-07:00","id":1482526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482521#post1482521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems interesting, the part of elders powers that doesn't make much sense in masquerade, I mean with Dominate 8 I can dominate any person in the world, one could dominate Biden and tell him to do anything I in the confort of my coffin, while a vampire with Fortitude 8 might still struggle in combat against a pack of Garous or gangrels, all because the system failed to come up with any decent power for the discipline level. I don't know much about Requiem, but the more I heard from it lately, the more I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Frankly, It's an all around better system than masquerade (V20 and V5), most people stick with masquerade because of the metaplot and for nostalgia's sake (I'm one of them btw, I grew up with masquerade) but aside from that, there really is no reason not switch to requiem beside personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T16:16:39-07:00","id":1482549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482521#post1482521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems interesting, the part of elders powers that doesn't make much sense in masquerade, I mean with Dominate 8 I can dominate any person in the world, one could dominate Biden and tell him to do anything I in the confort of my coffin, while a vampire with Fortitude 8 might still struggle in combat against a pack of Garous or gangrels, all because the system failed to come up with any decent power for the discipline level. I don't know much about Requiem, but the more I heard from it lately, the more I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specially on Second Edition it has more solid Innate Powers, better Discipline mechanics, and the Devotions.<br /> <br /> At first you'll find it lacks Elder Level powers, but just being able to pump more blood per turn gives you more options than in Masquerade, and Devotions with high BP as a requisite are a thing, they basically make for Elder Powers.<br /> <br /> The only limit on porting any or all of its rule to Masquerade is your willingness to introduce changes into an ongoing chronicle, specially for the Disciplines as they have too many mechanical changes (I encourage porting at least Fortitude and Protean).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T20:10:05-07:00","id":1482567,"title":"","content":"Vampire flesh being 'just as durable as steel' doesn't mean you suddenly got sheathed in vibranium. Steel can still be deformed and damaged in lots of ways (especialyl depending on the properties of the steel. Tool steel and mild steels will have very different properties as they trade off on things like strength/hardness, ductility, etc.) It also isn't at all clear what 'mundane' means either ('mundane temperatures' don't incldue a 'tongue of flame' so its clearly not immunity to all heat/fire even outside of combat) so there's alot of ambiguity that means you can play all kinds of semantics games (or worse, rules lawyering) but I find alot of power descriptions can run into this problem. <br /> <br /> As Prometheas said, you could rationalize it as applying only to the hands (alot of the activities specify that) or you could assume combat and noncombat situations have different requirements in terms of mobility, concentration, etc. Having your skin be thick, rigid, high hardness tool steel is probably going to cause alot of problems with your agility, unless you go for something softer, thinner, more flexible. But if you do that then you probably are compromising some of the protective value. Alternately, the level of concentration required to maintain the 'resilience' is harder IN combat (when you're under threat by one or more opponents) rather than out of combat (where you aren't necessarily under that kind of strain) and so you run into different limitations. <br /> <br /> And yes, I suppose you could just take the 'steel' bit less literally, or handwave the 'realism' aspects of the material properties of steels or metals... but if you're doing that you can do that for all the other problems too.<br /> <br /> Really I'm not seeing any problems unless one insists on forcing very specific meanings/definitions on how the passage is to be interpreted, and you could literally spend pages arguing over the semantics without outside clarification. And this being the internet, I'm sure there are people who can do that (or may have even done it in the past.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T06:23:02-07:00","id":1482596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482549#post1482549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specially on Second Edition it has more solid Innate Powers, better Discipline mechanics, and the Devotions.<br /> <br /> At first you'll find it lacks Elder Level powers, but just being able to pump more blood per turn gives you more options than in Masquerade, and Devotions with high BP as a requisite are a thing, they basically make for Elder Powers.<br /> <br /> The only limit on porting any or all of its rule to Masquerade is your willingness to introduce changes into an ongoing chronicle, specially for the Disciplines as they have too many mechanical changes (I encourage porting at least Fortitude and Protean).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I'm thinking about porting some of its powers as they are, as you mentioned, more solid. Talking about porting, I still need to read Protean in Requiem, I still haven't read it. All in all the system seems more polished, the thing that ties me to WoD is mostly the metaplot and nostalgia as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a> mentioned. Because from all I have read, most power mechanics are simply straight better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T06:47:59-07:00","id":1482598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482596#post1482596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I'm thinking about porting some of its powers as they are, as you mentioned, more solid. Talking about porting, I still need to read Protean in Requiem, I still haven't read it. All in all the system seems more polished, the thing that ties me to WoD is mostly the metaplot and nostalgia as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a> mentioned. Because from all I have read, most power mechanics are simply straight better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you feel you are up to it, you could just use the WoD metaplot with requiem's system, to be honest it wouldn't even be that difficult since requiem is made to be modular so you can do whatever the hell you want with the setting. I would suggest you take a look at requiem's lore too, despite its reputation as a barebone system, there is actually a rich backstory with plenty of hooks and the supplements have been, for the most part, superb, damnation city for 1st ed in particular should be an essential book for both WoD and Requiem, it has minimal mechanics but plenty of plot hooks and suggestions to run a vampire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:15:46-07:00","id":1482621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482598#post1482598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you feel you are up to it, you could just use the WoD metaplot with requiem's system, to be honest it wouldn't even be that difficult since requiem is made to be modular so you can do whatever the hell you want with the setting. I would suggest you take a look at requiem's lore too, despite its reputation as a barebone system, there is actually a rich backstory with plenty of hooks and the supplements have been, for the most part, superb, damnation city for 1st ed in particular should be an essential book for both WoD and Requiem, it has minimal mechanics but plenty of plot hooks and suggestions to run a vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great tip, I'll sure have a look at it. I guess I'd have to talk with my groups about it, and first and foremost I need to understand the system well in order to make it work. This tip of yours also makes me curious, I'm gonna look for this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:18:52-07:00","id":1482623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482621#post1482621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Great tip, I'll sure have a look at it. I guess I'd have to talk with my groups about it, and first and foremost I need to understand the system well in order to make it work. This tip of yours also makes me curious, I'm gonna look for this book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good luck, the conditions are a pain in the ass at first but you get used to it, just remember to keep the core book index at the ready and you will be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:35:39-07:00","id":1482627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482623#post1482623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Good luck, the conditions are a pain in the ass at first but you get used to it, just remember to keep the core book index at the ready and you will be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! It'll be funny if what finally makes me convert to the Storytelling is the lack of a way to represent vampire's supernatural resiliency in the Storyteller system.<br /> I mean I saw when they started the new WoD and I said &quot;no, no and no&quot; as I was since a kid in love with the Storyteller system, even though, much more due to the setting that I REALLY love, I mean the metaplot in the WoD is beyond anythng I've seen in any other RPG, but on the other side, I've always felt vampires are WAY TOO SQUISHY in the Storyteller system, it's like they're made of butter lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:00:29-07:00","id":1482631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482627#post1482627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you! It'll be funny if what finally makes me convert to the Storytelling is the lack of a way to represent vampire's supernatural resiliency in the Storyteller system.<br /> I mean I saw when they started the new WoD and I said &quot;no, no and no&quot; as I was since a kid in love with the Storyteller system, even though, much more due to the setting that I REALLY love, I mean the metaplot in the WoD is beyond anythng I've seen in any other RPG, but on the other side, I've always felt vampires are WAY TOO SQUISHY in the Storyteller system, it's like they're made of butter lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vamps in requiem are not squishy when put against humans but they still suffer from being the first game of the line, the other supernaturals are therefore more powerful although not to the exent of WOD where they are outclassed by practically everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:28:26-07:00","id":1482636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482631#post1482631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vamps in requiem are not squishy when put against humans but they still suffer from being the first game of the line, the other supernaturals are therefore more powerful although not to the exent of WOD where they are outclassed by practically everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, in WoD vampires suffer a lot from having a &quot;ceiling&quot; in the form of generation, so while theoretically <i>some</i> vampires are among the most powerful creatures in the world, I mean in the form of Methuselah and Antediluvian, the average player character is by far the weakest. Even then, Methuselah suffer from a set of &quot;not so well-developed&quot; defensive powers, to use a light term. Especially since Fortitude is by far the worst physical discipline vampires have access to. So, as I say, even Ur-Shulgi could be beaten by a pack of &quot;nobodies&quot; werewolves, just because the system doesn't cover up the said power of such a being has in the metaplot. IMO, it could be fixed with some simple adjustments, like allowing aggravated damage to be soaked with both Fortitude and Stamina and giving Fortitude some decent powers. It's even funny because RAW Fortitude is so bad, that Protean offers much better defensive powers, hell even Thaumaturgy is better for defense, with rituals that give the character extra soak dice (a level 1 btw, that could naturally be &quot;upgraded&quot; to a better and higher level version) or allow characters to soak fire damage, etc.<br /> I always make such adjustments, because I'm used to ST crossovers and as I love to dwell in other night folks lore, such as mage and werewolf, and lately changeling, I know that adjustments are very necessary to have a &quot;healthy&quot; game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:35:53-07:00","id":1482637,"title":"","content":"They're far less squishy in Requiem 2nd, even without Disciplines. To begin with, they're far harder to cause even Lethal to, much less Aggravated. Things like actually seeing well in the darkness, being able to track and identify blood better than a hound, and unleash your predatory aura as a weapon are nice, too, as innate abilities. The better defined resistance Disciplines are just icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> Either way, you can port the pieces little by little, and the similarities between the systems means that evenn without reading it entirely you can get the gist of most things. I think the biggest difference in the specific regard of Fortitude/Resilience is that Requiem gives Stamina as extra Health Levels instead of having a Soaking pool, but also makes avoiding the attacks in the first a default thing, so most of the time the attacker won't have a full attack pool and may even have a very tiny one, without need to declare an action for defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:42:14-07:00","id":1482640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482637#post1482637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're far less squishy in Requiem 2nd, even without Disciplines. To begin with, they're far harder to cause even Lethal to, much less Aggravated. Things like actually seeing well in the darkness, being able to track and identify blood better than a hound, and unleash your predatory aura as a weapon are nice, too, as innate abilities. The better defined resistance Disciplines are just icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> Either way, you can port the pieces little by little, and the similarities between the systems means that evenn without reading it entirely you can get the gist of most things. I think the biggest difference in the specific regard of Fortitude/Resilience is that Requiem gives Stamina as extra Health Levels instead of having a Soaking pool, but also makes avoiding the attacks in the first a default thing, so most of the time the attacker won't have a full attack pool and may even have a very tiny one, without need to declare an action for defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems in fact very interesting. I'll have to look at how Resilence and Stamina work in Requiem, etc. So I can better adapt it to my table, as we're very used to adjustments, I think I just need to read and get a better grasp of the system to port it to my tables. My players are kinda used to &quot;new patch coming&quot; announcements <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you all for the suggestions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:43:31-07:00","id":1482641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To begin with, they're far harder to cause even Lethal to, much less Aggravated </div> </div> </div>This part in particular, made me curious as it's something that applies to everyone, including the players and not just the NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:47:48-07:00","id":1482642,"title":"","content":"Another thing that requiem vamps have over masquerade is that they can learn most of the disciplines without a teacher and without having to taste blood, the clan specific disciplines are only 5 (protean, dominate, majesty, auspex and nightmare) and are the exception but resilience, celerity, vigor (requiem version of potency), animalism and obfuscate are available to everyone, this allows for much better customization compared to masquerade. A disadvantage they have over masquerade is that, once in torpor, any damage can do them in easily meaning that stomping on a torpored vamp is enough to do it in, this means that being torpored even against humans, is a death sentence while in masquerade (v20 and revised) it takes aggravated or decapitation to permanently kill a vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:50:48-07:00","id":1482643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482641#post1482641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part in particular, made me curious as it's something that applies to everyone, including the players and not just the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember that humans in CoD are much tougher than WoD, vamps take bashing from pretty much anything that isn't fire or supernatural in origin but a skilled human with an assault rifle can still ruin your day (unless you have celerity or resilience that is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T13:26:12-07:00","id":1482649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they can learn most of the disciplines without a teacher and without having to taste blood, the clan specific disciplines are only 5 (protean, dominate, majesty, auspex and nightmare) and are the exception but resilience, celerity, vigor (requiem version of potency), animalism and obfuscate are available to everyone </div> </div> </div>Regarding access to disciplines, I am in general very &quot;liberal&quot;. I allow all physical disciplines to be easily learned without a teacher as well, the part about animalism and obfuscate could be implemented as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> vamps take bashing from pretty much anything that isn't fire or supernatural </div> </div> </div>This is very interesting as well and I'm thinking about implementing it, as if there's something vampires should always be at the very least, it's resilient.. I'll probably change the system where it's &quot;better&quot; and keep with the lore of WoD, as I really love it. In any case, I now want to read the book you mentioned, the only book from the NwoD I remember really reading was &quot;Antagonists&quot;, many years ago. It had many interesting ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:09:41-07:00","id":1482667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482649#post1482649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding access to disciplines, I am in general very &quot;liberal&quot;. I allow all physical disciplines to be easily learned without a teacher as well, the part about animalism and obfuscate could be implemented as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is very interesting as well and I'm thinking about implementing it, as if there's something vampires should always be at the very least, it's resilient.. I'll probably change the system where it's &quot;better&quot; and keep with the lore of WoD, as I really love it. In any case, I now want to read the book you mentioned, the only book from the NwoD I remember really reading was &quot;Antagonists&quot;, many years ago. It had many interesting ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you are sticking with vampires the conversion could be almost painless but if you think about introducing other splats (most likely werewolf since in WoD they hate vamps which is not the case in CoD) there could be problems since they use an entirely different system for everything, vampire is pretty much the only one who kept things fairly similar, other CoD titles have changed pretty much everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T16:16:09-07:00","id":1482678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> most likely werewolf since in WoD they hate vamps which is not the case in CoD </div> </div> </div>That's very interesting to know! With the very rare exceptions like Vancouver, it seems every werewolf hates vampires in WoD. I'm curious now to understand their relationship in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T16:37:14-07:00","id":1482679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482678#post1482678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's very interesting to know! With the very rare exceptions like Vancouver, it seems every werewolf hates vampires in WoD. I'm curious now to understand their relationship in CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's mostly about them not really caring about eachother that much, they have their own crap to deal with, some werewolves hunt vampires but it's generally kept to specific vamps, even if werewolves are the combat splat of CoC, silver is much more distruptive and they don't gave any gift to defend against it so they are far less inclined to mess with other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T19:51:49-07:00","id":1482706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I've always felt vampires are WAY TOO SQUISHY in the Storyteller system, it's like they're made of butter lol </div> </div> </div>I did most of my playing in 2nd Edition, when the system was still to add Stamina to Fortitude for soak rolls except against fire and sunlight, and it took an aggravated wound to a vampire with no blood points or health levels left to destroy one. They were damn difficult to kill even for other supernaturals, though incapacitating them was somewhat more feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T20:30:56-07:00","id":1482710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482706#post1482706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did most of my playing in 2nd Edition, when the system was still to add Stamina to Fortitude for soak rolls except against fire and sunlight, and it took an aggravated wound to a vampire with no blood points or health levels left to destroy one. They were damn difficult to kill even for other supernaturals, though incapacitating them was somewhat more feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting thing that, to be fair, I didn't even remember. I played more with revised since I bought all the books when I was a kid. I never had a volume of Vampire The Masquerade 1st or 2nd edition. I thank thee for the useful tip, that is most definitely going to be useful and implemented as well. I'm kind of tired of TPKs lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T01:06:32-07:00","id":1482719,"title":"","content":"Yeah, getting torpored in masquerade wasn't a big deal, even in V5 you need to do some serious damage to finally destroy a vampire, in requiem on the other hand vampires are pretty damn hard to put down but torpor is pretty much a death sentence, by RAW a human with a dot in strength and no combat skills could just keep stomping on you and kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:57:24-07:00","id":1482785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482679#post1482679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly about them not really caring about eachother that much, they have their own crap to deal with, some werewolves hunt vampires but it's generally kept to specific vamps, even if werewolves are the combat splat of CoC, silver is much more distruptive and they don't gave any gift to defend against it so they are far less inclined to mess with other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't so much say they don't care, it is more that it is up in the air to the specific individuals and location. Most Main Splat interactions in CoD are undefined, it depends a lot on the specifics of a given region and the individuals involved. You can have alliances, rivalries, truces, businesses, in some places they may form a unified supernatural community and in other be at total war.<br /> <br /> You may even have cross-splat organizations, cities where political affiliations matter more than splat, and most of them have relatively open rules for affiliation in the in-splat groups, so you can run crossover parties from the core books out of the bat. The rules for Packs in Werewolf: the Forsaken come to mind, you can have anyone as a member and benefit from totem and Pack Rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:59:54-07:00","id":1482786,"title":"","content":"For how tough a character is once in Torpor, in my experience it doesn't make a lot of a difference. In all cases you get into Torpor long before you're actually killed, and that means you're helpless. Making it more or less hard to kill you them doesn't matter much, because your assailant either has to deal with your allies first or has all the time in the world to kill you, so what's the big difference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:27:20-07:00","id":1482790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, torpor if the vampire is alone, is basically a &quot;death sentence&quot; anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T11:51:06-07:00","id":1482806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482786#post1482786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For how tough a character is once in Torpor, in my experience it doesn't make a lot of a difference. In all cases you get into Torpor long before you're actually killed, and that means you're helpless. Making it more or less hard to kill you them doesn't matter much, because your assailant either has to deal with your allies first or has all the time in the world to kill you, so what's the big difference?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference is that in masquerade, unless your enemies came prepared, it would be almost impossible to destroy you right there and then, damage didn't wrap around in masquerade (don't know if they changed it later though) so the only way to do aggravated was to either have a supernatural ability ready or enough gasoline at handy for a small bonfire, same thing with decapitation, in short randos in the street weren't going to kill you even when torpored while in requiem, by RAW, an unarmed human with 1 strength and no combat skills can pretty much pitifully slap you into final death (I unfortunately had such an experience in a game and the ST didn't know how to portray my character's death since I was done in by an old lady with her handbag).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:05:47-07:00","id":1482808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482806#post1482806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (I unfortunately had such an experience in a game and the ST didn't know how to portray my character's death since I was done in by an old lady with her handbag).</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but I think you underestimate how hard an old lady with a handbag can hit. <br /> <br /> Of course, that depends on how much anger they have inside them, and just what they carry in their handbag...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:23:27-07:00","id":1482812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482808#post1482808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense, but I think you underestimate how hard an old lady with a handbag can hit.<br /> <br /> Of course, that depends on how much anger they have inside them, and just what they carry in their handbag...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hard enough to utterly destroy and immortal predator of the night? I also suggested that she might have had a brick inside of it but ST said that it was just silly so my character simply disappeared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T13:49:34-07:00","id":1482825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482806#post1482806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that in masquerade, unless your enemies came prepared, it would be almost impossible to destroy you right there and then, damage didn't wrap around in masquerade (don't know if they changed it later though) so the only way to do aggravated was to either have a supernatural ability ready or enough gasoline at handy for a small bonfire, same thing with decapitation, in short randos in the street weren't going to kill you even when torpored while in requiem, by RAW, an unarmed human with 1 strength and no combat skills can pretty much pitifully slap you into final death (I unfortunately had such an experience in a game and the ST didn't know how to portray my character's death since I was done in by an old lady with her handbag).</div> </div> </div> </div>In short, your ST either shouldn't had done that or it wouldn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> You're helpless. Full stop helpless, and without help will be so for days, at least. From there, we have a few likely scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1 - Your assailant doesn't know that you're a Vampire or doesn't really care to kill you. Once you're in torpor you're dead for all purposes in the immediate future. Why on Earth would they keep attacking you?<br /> <br /> 2 - Your assailant does know, or alternatively wants to get rid of evidence, A.K.A. your corpse. You're as able to resist as a sandbag for the foreseeable future, so being immediately unable to incinerate you just means they take their time to get your sorry ass to somewhere else where they can incinerate you;<br /> <br /> 3 - Your assailant wants to get rid of you, but is under a time constraint. A random thug will think you're dead, so won't care to keep hitting you, that's utterly pointless, they'll just hide the corpse. Someone in the know and with a will to kill is likely to have the means at hand. If they don't and the time constraint is really important, they'll either kidnap you and solve the constraint or leave you be, because they still have a frigging time constraint.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, for this to be a relevant factor you need an enemy that A) knows what you are, B) wants to kill you, C) isn't regularly prepared to deal with vampires, D) got the opportunity unexpectedly, so they're utterly unprepared and E) has a time constraint that's long enough to keep attacking you, but not enough to just grab you and leave.<br /> <br /> Not really impossible to come by, but it's still an extremely contrived set of circumstances, really unlikely to happen. What you ST did, and this isn't uncommon, was probably get carried by the rules and miss the point of the action entirely. That, or that old lady was a Hunter that either had the means to off you in her handbag or was at this precise unlikely set of circumstances.<br /> <br /> That's why, in the end, it matters little how hard vampires are to kill after going into torpor, as long as it is hard enough to be unlikely to go from awake to destroyed in the same event, in comparison to how hard it is to put them in torpor in the first place, and that's why the authors found it simpler to not worry too much about the matter. A Requiem Vampire is tougher in this regard because they'll shrug a lot more damage and still function to be able to get the Hell away out of Dodge or off their assailant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T14:09:57-07:00","id":1482829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482825#post1482825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, your ST either shouldn't had done that or it wouldn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> You're helpless. Full stop helpless, and without help will be so for days, at least. From there, we have a few likely scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1 - Your assailant doesn't know that you're a Vampire or doesn't really care to kill you. Once you're in torpor you're dead for all purposes in the immediate future. Why on Earth would they keep attacking you?<br /> <br /> 2 - Your assailant does know, or alternatively wants to get rid of evidence, A.K.A. your corpse. You're as able to resist as a sandbag for the foreseeable future, so being immediately unable to incinerate you just means they take their time to get your sorry ass to somewhere else where they can incinerate you;<br /> <br /> 3 - Your assailant wants to get rid of you, but is under a time constraint. A random thug will think you're dead, so won't care to keep hitting you, that's utterly pointless, they'll just hide the corpse. Someone in the know and with a will to kill is likely to have the means at hand. If they don't and the time constraint is really important, they'll either kidnap you and solve the constraint or leave you be, because they still have a frigging time constraint.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, for this to be a relevant factor you need an enemy that A) knows what you are, B) wants to kill you, C) isn't regularly prepared to deal with vampires, D) got the opportunity unexpectedly, so they're utterly unprepared and E) has a time constraint that's long enough to keep attacking you, but not enough to just grab you and leave.<br /> <br /> Not really impossible to come by, but it's still an extremely contrived set of circumstances, really unlikely to happen. What you ST did, and this isn't uncommon, was probably get carried by the rules and miss the point of the action entirely. That, or that old lady was a Hunter that either had the means to off you in her handbag or was at this precise unlikely set of circumstances.<br /> <br /> That's why, in the end, it matters little how hard vampires are to kill after going into torpor, as long as it is hard enough to be unlikely to go from awake to destroyed in the same event, in comparison to how hard it is to put them in torpor in the first place, and that's why the authors found it simpler to not worry too much about the matter. A Requiem Vampire is tougher in this regard because they'll shrug a lot more damage and still function to be able to get the Hell away out of Dodge or off their assailant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are missing another scenario: You are torpored in the middle of a fight, they know who you are, your friends are nearby and ready to defend you, at this point in masquerade they would most likely be able help you since the opponents, realizing that they don't have the means and the time to end your unlife quickly, will either flee or be disposed of, in requiem instead the hunter who torpored you, seeing your buddies coming, will simply take a turn and use a death blow on you with his peashooter, voil\u00e0, 12 points of aggravated and the big bad vamp died by being shot with a .22, see what I mean with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T14:50:39-07:00","id":1482836,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty confident most of us here get your point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a>. It's just that... Sometimes shit happens. &quot;Goldlike&quot; Antediluvians still got diablerized, one of them by MAGES instead of vampires.<br /> <br /> Try to look at it this way; the Titanic didn't just sink because she hit an iceberg. She sunk because she was going at full steam when she hit an iceberg the lookouts couldn't see in time because the ship didn't get the binoculars before launching, and the helmsman didn't hear about it in time because everyone was SO CONVINCED the boat was unsinkable, the telegraph officer responded to iceberg warnings with &quot;Stop bothering me, I'm busy.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is your &quot;big, bad vamp&quot; didn't just meet final death because of a .22. He got dusted by a .22 AFTER being beaten into a bloody torpor! By someone with Potence, or Protean, or maybe &quot;just&quot; the ability to shift into a 9 foot Garou form strong enough to rip out a manhole cover and club you into the concrete with it. Or to grab you by your legs and swing you like a club into the concrete until you're buried halfway.<br /> <br /> It isn't JUST the straw that breaks the camel's back, it's the straw, AND the water jugs, AND the loaded sacks, AND the luggage trunks, AND the anvils...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-02-2022, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T15:22:29-07:00","id":1482840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482829#post1482829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">see what I mean with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that you're still holding to the fact that such scenarios exist instead of how likely they are.<br /> <br /> A Hunter under such circumstances falls neatly into the 3rd scenario I described, and is likely to have other tools at hand to off you, after all they're a hunter. They may not even know that a gun is enough once you're torpid either way. And again, how frequently such a scenario is? You're already under the hands of a hunter, they got to put you in torpor, yet your friends are arriving just in time to invalidate any other option than a gun shot, neither soon enough to take a part in the battle or late enough for the hunter to use a more classical method.<br /> <br /> That <b><u>is</u> </b>an extremely contrived circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  missing space 06-02-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T15:46:21-07:00","id":1482846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482840#post1482840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that you're still holding to the fact that such scenarios exist instead of how likely they are.<br /> <br /> A Hunter under such circumstances falls neatly into the 3rd scenario I described, and is likely to have other tools at hand to off you, after all they're a hunter. They may not even know that a gun is enough once you're torpid either way. And again, how frequently such a scenario is? You're already under the hands of a hunter, they got to put you in torpor, yet your friends are arriving just in time to invalidate any other option than a gun shot, neither soon enough to take a part in the battle or late enough for the hunter to use a more classical method.<br /> <br /> That <b><u>is</u> </b>an extremely contrived circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are missing my point, your scenarios fail to account the time it requires to properly finish off a torpored masquerade vamp vs how easy it is to do so to a torpored one in requiem, another easy and not contrived example: You get into a fight with the cops, normal ones who don't know anything about vampires, they shoot you and you don't stay dead, so they think you are on pcp or something and keep shooting you well after you have entered torpor, masquerade vamp is torpored but not dead so the rest of the coterie can still sneak you out of the morgue or something, requiem vamp meanwhile is utterly dusted becaue the system has damage wrap around see the difference here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T15:55:16-07:00","id":1482848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482846#post1482846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are missing my point, your scenarios fail to account the time it requires to properly finish off a torpored masquerade vamp vs how easy it is to do so to a torpored one in requiem, another easy and not contrived example: You get into a fight with the cops, normal ones who don't know anything about vampires, they shoot you and you don't stay dead, so they think you are on pcp or something and keep shooting you well after you have entered torpor, masquerade vamp is torpored but not dead so the rest of the coterie can still sneak you out of the morgue or something, requiem vamp meanwhile is utterly dusted becaue the system has damage wrap around see the difference here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not missing your point, we're just not on the same page here at all. At this point we'll just iterate the same arguments again as I look at this example and see the exact same problems of the last one.<br /> <br /> You have a point, it is a lot easier. In my experience it will make a difference once in a blue moon or less, yours may differ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T16:20:54-07:00","id":1482850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482846#post1482846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You are missing my point, your scenarios fail to account the time it requires to properly finish off a torpored masquerade vamp vs how easy it is to do so to a torpored one in requiem, another easy and not contrived example: You get into a fight with the cops, normal ones who don't know anything about vampires, they shoot you and you don't stay dead, so they think you are on pcp or something and keep shooting you well after you have entered torpor, masquerade vamp is torpored but not dead so the rest of the coterie can still sneak you out of the morgue or something, requiem vamp meanwhile is utterly dusted becaue the system has damage wrap around see the difference here?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I missed the part in your scenario where your &quot;Big Bad Vamp&quot; was fighting Hunters instead of Kindred or Garou. I'm sorry about that. But the thing is, your &quot;big bad vamp&quot; STILL get's beaten into torpor. THAT's the problem, NOT the .22. If someone was committed enough to dust your &quot;big bad vamp&quot; that they damage him into bloody topor, they're not going to stop just because that Vampire's friends are standing on the side looking scary.<br /> <br /> You seem to want us to agree with you that the rules are the problem, but I have to say the problem is with the Vampire's &quot;friends.&quot; If they're so &quot;ready to defend you,&quot; why don't they at least put themselves between the torpored Vampire and the Hunters?<br /> <br /> Whether you're a thin-blooded neonate or bloody Caine himself, everyone's a gangster, UNTIL they go into torpor. Then, they are FORMER gangsters. Get the drift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:17:52-07:00","id":1482862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482850#post1482850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I missed the part in your scenario where your &quot;Big Bad Vamp&quot; was fighting Hunters instead of Kindred or Garou. I'm sorry about that. But the thing is, your &quot;big bad vamp&quot; STILL get's beaten into torpor. THAT's the problem, NOT the .22. If someone was committed enough to dust your &quot;big bad vamp&quot; that they damage him into bloody topor, they're not going to stop just because that Vampire's friends are standing on the side looking scary.<br /> <br /> You seem to want us to agree with you that the rules are the problem, but I have to say the problem is with the Vampire's &quot;friends.&quot; If they're so &quot;ready to defend you,&quot; why don't they at least put themselves between the torpored Vampire and the Hunters?<br /> <br /> Whether you're a thin-blooded neonate or bloody Caine himself, everyone's a gangster, UNTIL they go into torpor. Then, they are FORMER gangsters. Get the drift?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You too are missing the point, the friends example wasn't about the rest of the coterie standing around like morons while the vamp is getting murdered, they would start shooting or close the distance to attack, the difference is right there, in masquerade they wouldn't have the time to finish you off (unless they have a flamethrower that is) because it takes time to properly kill a vamp (at least for humans, supernaturals are another matter) since you have to set them on fire or chop off their head (which is really not supported by any mechanics save for a few obscure supplements from the 90's) while in requiem it literally takes a turn which is 3 seconds because the system in there has wrap around damage meaning that, when the health boxes are full of one kind of damage, like bashing for example, and you do another point of bashing, the damage gets upgraded to lethal and upward to aggravated, this means that a totally normal human can kill a torpored vampire with his bare hands which is just not possible in masquerade.<br /> <br /> This whole discussion wasn't about weather or not something is possible, this is about mechanics and mechanically, vampires in requiem are easier to kill when in torpor then vampires in masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:20:38-07:00","id":1482864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482848#post1482848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not missing your point, we're just not on the same page here at all. At this point we'll just iterate the same arguments again as I look at this example and see the exact same problems of the last one.<br /> <br /> You have a point, it is a lot easier. In my experience it will make a difference once in a blue moon or less, yours may differ.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My reasoning is not whether or not something is likely from storytelling standpoint but purely from a mechanical one and the mechanics say that is a lot easier to dust a torpored vamp in requiem compared to masquerade, that is all I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:47:27-07:00","id":1482871,"title":"","content":"Well, at least they're harder to put down, what is a great start since in VtM it's hard to imagine the average pc vampire to survive a turn against another supernatural creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T18:26:04-07:00","id":1482877,"title":"","content":"But, in the end, there's not much a cainite can do in torpor.*<br /> <br /> *Edit: I mean for the &quot;average joe&quot; cainite, not blood gods like Mithras, Ur-Shulgi, The Capuchin or Tremere lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-02-2022, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T09:36:01-07:00","id":1482941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482864#post1482864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reasoning is not whether or not something is likely from storytelling standpoint but purely from a mechanical one and the mechanics say that is a lot easier to dust a torpored vamp in requiem compared to masquerade, that is all I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, just to confirm about one rule doubt you admitted to from the beginning: the wrap-around damage is present since <i>V20</i>, so your reasoning refers only to 1st and 2nd edition. While the easier kill is true for Requiem, it is also true for Masquerade from mid 2011 onward.<br /> <br /> Second, I got your reasoning a long time ago and agreed to it, <b>my</b> point wasn't about it not being true, it was about it not being relevant. And while I completely agree with differing mechanics and lore, the likelihood of a given situation is a relevant matter for mechanics' design, so it is still relevant even from a purely mechanical standpoint.<br /> <br /> I stand to my point that, while true, the relative fragility once in torpor isn't a relevant problem because the scenarios where it would actually play out are considerably specific and unlikely under most STs I know of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also to add, Requiem required the rule on rolling damage because dealing Aggravated became far harder there, and also became standard for <b>everyone</b> to only die at full Agg, making even mortals a bit more resilient between hospitalization and death.<br /> <br /> It also compensates that while Masquerade required Aggravated to finish a torpid vampire, it only required <b>ONE</b> level of damage, while Requiem requires a full track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 06-03-2022, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T10:10:34-07:00","id":1482943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308322-armored-flesh?p=1482941#post1482941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, just to confirm about one rule doubt you admitted to from the beginning: the wrap-around damage is present since <i>V20</i>, so your reasoning refers only to 1st and 2nd edition. While the easier kill is true for Requiem, it is also true for Masquerade from mid 2011 onward.<br /> <br /> Second, I got your reasoning a long time ago and agreed to it, <b>my</b> point wasn't about it not being true, it was about it not being relevant. And while I completely agree with differing mechanics and lore, the likelihood of a given situation is a relevant matter for mechanics' design, so it is still relevant even from a purely mechanical standpoint.<br /> <br /> I stand to my point that, while true, the relative fragility once in torpor isn't a relevant problem because the scenarios where it would actually play out are considerably specific and unlikely under most STs I know of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also to add, Requiem required the rule on rolling damage because dealing Aggravated became far harder there, and also became standard for <b>everyone</b> to only die at full Agg, making even mortals a bit more resilient between hospitalization and death.<br /> <br /> It also compensates that while Masquerade required Aggravated to finish a torpid vampire, it only required <b>ONE</b> level of damage, while Requiem requires a full track.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where did you read that they changed it in V20? I just read the book now and didn't see anything about wrap around damage, was it in an errata or something?<br /> <br /> I also got your point but that was irrelevant to my first post about torpor in masquerade, what I meant is that masquerade vamps were harder to destroy when in torpor then requiem vamp, just that, the likelyhood of a certain situation happening in game doesn't invalidate the truth of the statement, yes torpor is a death sentence most of the time but masquerade vamps have a few more chances to survive it (That is if they didn't change it in an errata or something, like I wrote before, I read the V20 core and the system is still the same.<br /> <br /> Requiem requiring a full track is also meaningless since the killing blow rule would apply and most characters would be able to destroy a vamp in a turn anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}